  "id": "COMPOUND:34435 - PROTEIN:4045",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol is implicated in the regulation of Pol polyprotein through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving the interaction with the Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1 and Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK. These targets are both directly engaged by Ent-Gloeosteretriol and lead to a downstream effect on Pol polyprotein. The evidence suggests that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may modulate Pol polyprotein through a series of molecular interactions, potentially affecting its function or activity. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on Pol polyprotein indicates a possible mechanism involving regulatory pathways that are sensitive to Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Ent-Gloeosteretriol exerts a functional influence on Pol polyprotein, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
